# Keep rules for the shipped APK, same job as glance-widgets.keep beside it: a class this app
# reaches by name rather than by symbol.
#
# YlihAppFunctionService is written by KSP from agent/YlihAppFunctions.kt and nothing in the
# source tree ever names it except the <service> element in the manifest. AAPT2 does generate a
# keep rule for a manifest component, so in principle this is insurance rather than a fix — but
# the component only exists once KSP has run, which is one more link in the chain than any other
# component in this manifest has, and the failure it protects against is invisible: a renamed
# service still installs, and the OS simply never binds it. The app functions would then be
# advertised and uncallable, which reads as an agent that ignores the app.
#
# .github/scripts/r8-keep-check.py asserts it survives under this name on every push.
-keep class it.eldavo.ylih.agent.YlihAppFunctionService
